{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>From twenty years old unto sixty years old.</b> It would have been fitting for the verses to be ordered: if from a month old unto five years old, and if from five years old unto twenty years old, and if from twenty years old unto sixty years old, and if from sixty years old and upward, if a male, and the conclusion of the passage. But because the passage began ״איש כי יפליא״ — 'when a man makes a singular vow' — it was necessary to begin from twenty years old, for a month-old and a five-year-old are minors and not איש; and moreover they do not evaluate themselves, but rather the adult says, 'the valuation of this month-old is upon me,' or 'the valuation of this five-year-old is upon me.' And once it began from twenty, it needed to arrange 'if from five unto twenty,' which it had begun with, and then it says afterward 'and if from a month old unto five years old,' which it had begun with, and then it says afterward 'and if from sixty years old and upward.' Thus explained the Ramban, of blessed memory."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:28:56.793307158Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}